      "date_text": "15 Sep - 1 Dec 2026",
      "description": "<p>\n\n          From modern Japanese gardens to experimental land art, wilderness and utopia to environmental hopes and anxieties, join us to stretch our ideas of what gardens and place can mean as artistic practice in an era of climate change. \n        </p>\n<p>\n\n          <p>This autumn at the Garden Museum, a new series of talks bringing together curators, gardeners, and artists exploring gardens, landscape, and environment as artistic practice.</p>\n<p>Across five evenings chaired and curated by landscape historian and critic Tim Richardson, hear from a range of practitioners, curators and academics discussing their own work and reflecting on the broader scene.</p>\n<p>A drink is included in the price of the ticket so stick around to continue the discussion. Book for all five evenings at a reduced price.</p>\n<p><strong>Please note that our talks now begin at 6:30pm, rather than 7pm, giving you more time to enjoy dinner at our award-winning Garden Museum Café. Table reservations are available <a data-cke-saved-href=\"http://www.sevenrooms.com/explore/gardenmuseum/reservations/create/search/\" href=\"http://www.sevenrooms.com/explore/gardenmuseum/reservations/create/search/\">here</a>. Your talk ticket also includes entry to the Garden Museum’s temporary exhibitions from 6pm on the evening of the talk.</strong></p>\n\n        </p>",
