      "date_text": "18 Oct 2026, 11am - 4pm",
      "description": "<p>\n\n          The Garden Museum Harvest Festival is a day of stalls, talks and workshops exploring the world of growing and producing food in the city. \n        </p>\n<p>\n\n          <p>For its third edition, the Garden Museum Harvest Festival 2026 – in collaboration with <em>felloe</em> – celebrates the people finding innovative, exciting ways to grow food in urban settings, across London and beyond.</p>\n<p>Cities now hold around 60% of the world’s population. As people have moved to urban settings, they’ve become increasingly dependent on long supply chains to access food grown far away.</p>\n<p>And yet, from community gardens that have transformed neglected land into neighbourhood hubs, to rooftop beehives, underground mushroom caves, vertical farms and windowsill fermentation jars, the world of urban growing is creative and sprawling, offering inspiring and novel ideas on how we can bring back our connection to food and growing to the cities so many of us now call home.</p>\n<p>Join us on Sunday 18 October for a day full of stalls, workshops and talks all about the world of urban growing.</p>\n<p>This year’s stalls will include: <a href=\"https://www.simplicitybakery.co.uk\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>Simplicity</strong></a>, <a href=\"https://e5bakehouse.com\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>E5 Bakehouse</strong></a>, <a href=\"https://www.theferm.net\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>The Ferm</strong></a>, <strong>The China Edit, </strong><a href=\"https://companydrinks.info\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>Company Drinks</strong></a>, <a href=\"https://garnakvass.com/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>Kvass</strong></a>, <a href=\"https://www.marysmarmalade.co.uk/\"><strong>Mary’s Marmalade</strong></a>, <a href=\"https://rootcodrinks.co.uk/?srsltid=AU7gw4XA9pC6Y7btY3De-FazzIO13sePrgUgIakokZn32VZztFUkXfeW\"><strong>The Root Co</strong></a>, <a href=\"https://kikefir.com/?srsltid=AU7gw4W-08AEPZw3IvQV8kiq_3r7LdV89uwBcK_keJL2KzcUzEFgLTE_\"><strong>Ki Kefir</strong></a>, <a href=\"https://www.lamiriharissa.com/\"><strong>Lamiri Harissa</strong></a>, <a href=\"https://uppaclub.com/?srsltid=AU7gw4UffTjHZvriW0yhv59CqEgilLt-3wJOHOZsrqySvsedQKCeFaHi\"><strong>Uppa Club</strong></a>, <strong>Vicky’s Noodles</strong></p>\n<p>We’re also delighted to present a programme of talks and activities curated by Amy Bendel, founder of <a href=\"https://www.felloe.co.uk/about\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Felloe,</a> and Ollie Whitehead, Head of Public Programmes at the Garden Museum. Please note, these talks and workshops must be booked separately in addition to the Harvest Festival entry ticket.</p>\n<p>The award-winning <a href=\"https://www.gardenmuseum.org.uk/visit/garden-cafe/\">Garden Café</a> will be open throughout the day serving a fresh, seasonal menu. Takeaway cakes and beverages will be available for walk-ins, booking is essential for lunch: <a href=\"https://www.gardenmuseum.org.uk/visit/garden-cafe/\">book a table</a></p>\n\n        </p>",
