      "description": "This Harvest Festival, join George Hudson and Divya Hariramani ( Fruity Walks ) for something a little different: a slow bicycle ride through South London’s overlooked green corners, tracing the trees growing along the way. The route winds from Lambeth’s riverside edges into quieter Georgian squares and community gardens further south: Vauxhall Walk Black Prince Road Imperial War Museum Garden West Square Cottington Community Alberta Fruits Commons Kennington Park Walworth Garden We’ll pause along the way to look up and share the stories of what’s growing at each stop, finishing at Walworth Garden. Expect a relaxed pace and plenty of stopping. Suitable for confident cyclists comfortable riding on quiet city roads. This talk is part of the Harvest Festival 2026 programme. In order to purchase this talk you must also purchase a general entry ticket for the Harvest Festival 2026.",
