      "date_text": "18 Oct 2026, 10am - 12pm",
      "description": "<p>\n\n          <p>This Harvest Festival, join George Hudson and Divya Hariramani (<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/fruitywalks/?hl=en\">Fruity Walks</a>) for something a little different: a slow bicycle ride through South London’s overlooked green corners, tracing the trees growing along the way.</p>\n<p>The route winds from Lambeth’s riverside edges into quieter Georgian squares and community gardens further south:</p>\n<p>Vauxhall Walk<br>\nBlack Prince Road<br>\nImperial War Museum Garden<br>\nWest Square<br>\nCottington Community<br>\nAlberta&nbsp;Fruits Commons<br>\nKennington Park<br>\nWalworth Garden</p>\n<p>We’ll pause along the way to look up and share the stories of what’s growing at each stop, finishing at Walworth Garden.</p>\n<p>Expect a relaxed pace and plenty of stopping. Suitable for confident cyclists comfortable riding on quiet city roads.</p>\n<p><strong>This talk is part of the Harvest Festival 2026&nbsp;programme. In order to purchase this talk you must also purchase a general entry ticket for the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://gardenmuseum.digitickets.co.uk/event-tickets/80057\">Harvest Festival 2026</a>.</strong></p>\n\n        </p>",
