      "date_text": "6 Oct 2026, 6:30pm - 7:30pm",
      "description": "<p>\n\n          <p>Grab a chair (and perhaps a trowel) for an evening with gardener and painter Matthew Rice, marking the launch of his new book,&nbsp;<em>A Year in the Garden</em>.</p>\n<p>14 years ago, Matthew bought the last shred of a medieval castle gatehouse in the very edge of the Cotswolds at Bampton. Move a decade forward and where there were concrete barns, slurry lagoons, and silage pits there is a walled garden, glasshouses, hen runs, and an orchard.</p>\n<p><em>A Year in the Garden</em>&nbsp;is a record of 12 months spent working, painting, and planning in a garden that is personal and flower filled and undisciplined but super productive. This evening Matthew will talk about the transformation and why he’s always reluctant to leave and joyful to get home.</p>\n<p><strong>Please note that our talks now begin at 6:30pm, rather than 7pm, giving you more time to enjoy dinner at our award-winning Garden Museum Cafe. Table reservations are available <a data-cke-saved-href=\"http://www.sevenrooms.com/explore/gardenmuseum/reservations/create/search/\" href=\"http://www.sevenrooms.com/explore/gardenmuseum/reservations/create/search/\">here</a>. Your talk ticket also includes entry to the Garden Museum’s temporary exhibitions from 6pm on the evening of the talk.</strong></p>\n\n        </p>",
