      "date_text": "10 Nov - 15 Nov 2026, 10am - 5pm",
      "description": "<p>\n\n          Every Winter Flowers Week we deck the halls of the Garden Museum with seasonal flowers and foliage, as we invite five floral designers transform the museum into a winter wonderland.\n        </p>\n<p>\n\n          <p>With sustainability at the heart, their installations will be created using only British-grown seasonal flowers and foliage, and environmentally-friendly materials and methods.</p>\n<p>This year’s exhibiting floral designers are Flùr, Billy Loves Flowers, Yinari, Botanical Tales and Joanne Truby, all trailblazers in the field and passionate about improving sustainability in the floristry industry. Meet the designers below!</p>\n<p>The week will also include a <a href=\"https://www.gardenmuseum.org.uk/whats-on/winter-flowers-week-2026-late/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Late</a> and <a href=\"https://www.gardenmuseum.org.uk/whats-on/winter-flowers-week-2025-meet-the-designers-panel-talk/\">panel talk</a> on Thursday 12 November, a chance to mingle among the flowers with a drink in hand, live music and floral activities.</p>\n\n        </p>",
